 ],
 "text": "Every level of using AI and where most people get stuck. Level 1. You ask it questions like a search engine. You get a decent answer, you copy it, and you rewrite half of it anyway. Level 2. You give it examples of your writing and your tone. Now the answers start sounding like you, not like a robot that swallowed a dictionary. Level 3. You give it your files, your prices, your past proposals, your notes. Now it actually knows your business. Level 4. You turn the stuff you repeat every week into skills. One sentence, and it does the whole task the same way every time. You never explain it twice. Level 5. It runs the work on its own. It drafts the replies, the invoices, and the posts, then waits for your yes before anything goes out. Most people never get past level 2. Comment AI, and I'll send you the 5 skills that get you to level 4, free."
